From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:28:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: JIT code caches take their direct memory in 2 MiB steps
 as the code grows

0.9.7. Each core's code cache was taken whole when the core was made: four caches of jit_cache_mib (256 MiB in the test settings) were 1 GiB of the
console's 4.5 GiB of direct memory held from the start for code that is a few tens of MiB. In the Mario Odyssey test the free direct block fell from
1242 MiB to 44 MiB in 90 s and the run ended in VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY, or in a guest page that could not be committed (SIGSEGV).

A cache is now only reserved address space (sceKernelReserveVirtualRange) and gets a 2 MiB step of direct memory (mapped fixed, then promoted to
RWX, the same order as before) when BlockOfCode::EnsureMemoryCommitted asks for it, which Dynarmic does before every block - the hook upstream uses
on Windows to commit code memory as it grows. The first two steps (the constant pool and the prelude) are taken with the block, so a kernel that
will not map or promote a step that way is found at once and the whole block is taken as before. Once the prelude is complete memory is taken a
little ahead of the code (a step is asked for while codesize + 1 MiB of room is left, and the cache is taken to codesize + 2 MiB past the code), because
Dynarmic checks SpaceRemaining() before EnsureMemoryCommitted and then writes a block into what it finds: a step the kernel refuses must still leave
that block its room. If a later step is refused the cache stops growing and is flushed when less than 1 MiB is left (SpaceRemaining honours the
limit), instead of writing past what it has.

ps4_jit_cache_lazy (set by the frontend before the cores are made, jit_cache_commit in settings.txt; 0 = the old way) and five counters for the
boot.log line: ps4_jit_chunks_large/small, ps4_jit_commit_failed, ps4_jit_reserved_bytes, ps4_jit_committed_bytes.

committed_size, orbis_limit and orbis_ahead are declared before constant_pool: its constructor calls EnsureMemoryCommitted while the object is being made.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PwQLQy9xSN2RjJRnq5bYjb
